                                                                            <comments>
                            <comment id="489931" author="tappro" created="Thu, 5 Mar 2026 04:37:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;One thing which need to be done at least - target should resend NID lists if notification request fails for some reason. The mgc_nid_notify_interpret() could trigger target NIDs notification in case of error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;check if import is full&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;check error code &lt;img class=&quot;emoticon&quot; src=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/images/icons/emoticons/help_16.png&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;call mgc_notify_active()/obd_notify_observer()&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;prevent loops like error-&amp;gt;resend-&amp;gt;same error-&amp;gt;...&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="493471" author="adilger" created="Mon, 20 Apr 2026 23:58:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=tappro&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;tappro&quot;&gt;tappro&lt;/a&gt;, in &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19917&quot; title=&quot;FTM: MGS replica imperative recovery support&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19917&quot;&gt;LU-19917&lt;/a&gt; Lai is adding MGS IR table replication across server nodes.  Currently this is one-way replication (primary MGS0 -&amp;gt; replica MGS), but for many purposes this is sufficient.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the primary MGS0 fails, then it could repopulate the IR table from one of the replicas during restart?  Maybe check a couple of them to see if they all have the same records.  This is essentially starting to look like RAFT...&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
